[00:00.00] 作词 : Ryan Met/Jack Met
[00:00.00][by:stillworkingonit]
[00:01.00] 作曲 : Ryan Met/Jack Met
[00:10.81]I turned twenty-nine over the weekend
[00:10.81]周末刚过 我二十九岁了
[00:16.14]You know you're not blocked, you still can call
[00:16.14]你知道自己没被拉黑 还可以打电话过来
[00:21.04]Did you hear we played the Garden?
[00:21.04]你有没有听说我们登上麦迪逊花园
[00:23.75]And I got my own apartment
[00:23.75]我有了自己的公寓
[00:27.94]Are you in touch with anyone at all?
[00:27.94]你和谁还有联系吗
[00:33.01]I bet you never ever sit in silence
[00:33.01]我料到 你永远不会静坐沉默
[00:37.90]You'll try therapists till one tells you you're great
[00:37.90]你会不停换心理医生 收到夸赞才罢休
[00:43.69]Or else it might get clear though
[00:43.69]不然的话 或许你会明白
[00:46.12]That you're not the ****ing hero
[00:46.12]你根本不是什么主角
[00:50.12]And if you called, I don't know what I'd say
[00:50.12]若你真致电过来 我也不知道该说什么
[00:55.36]I'm sorry you went crazy
[00:55.36]很遗憾 你没了理智
[01:00.70]I'm sorry that I'm saying it so blunt
[01:00.70]抱歉 我说得太直白
[01:06.30]Everybody says that you look happy
[01:06.30]人人都说 你看起来很幸福
[01:10.94]But to me
[01:10.94]但于我而言
[01:12.84]You just look like someone that I used to love
[01:12.84]你只是长得像我深爱过的那个人
[01:26.38]Okay, you're right!
[01:26.38]好吧 你说得对
[01:28.61]And we're all evil aliens
[01:28.61]我们都是邪恶外星人
[01:32.05]And thank God you're here to save the human race from us
[01:32.05]感谢有你拯救人类 免遭侵略
[01:37.40]So shoot me in my weak spot
[01:37.40]那就瞄准我的弱点
[01:39.97]With your subatomic laser gun
[01:39.97]用你亚原子激光枪射击
[01:45.21]Now you're really all alone
[01:45.21]如今你真的成了孤身一人
[01:48.49]I'm sorry you went crazy
[01:48.49]很遗憾 你没了理智
[01:53.75]I'm sorry that the money's what you want
[01:53.75]抱歉 你是个拜金狂
[01:59.34]Everybody says that you look happy
[01:59.34]人人都说 你看起来很幸福
[02:03.95]But to me
[02:03.95]但于我而言
[02:05.89]You just look like someone that I used to love
[02:05.89]你只是长得像我深爱过的那个人
[02:10.92]I'm sorry you went crazy
[02:10.92]很遗憾 你没了理智
[02:14.86]I'm sure it isn't any ****ing fun
[02:14.86]想必这绝不好受
[02:20.40]Yeah, you've gotten good at looking happy
[02:20.40]是啊 你多擅长向人展现假幸福
[02:25.10]But to me
[02:25.10]但于我而言
[02:26.99]You just look like someone that you used to love
[02:26.99]你只是长得像你爱过的那个自己
